Domain setup.

1. GitHub Pages settings in your repo
Set these values in GitHub:
- Source: Deploy from a branch
- Branch: main
- Folder: / (root)

Then save.

2. Custom domain in GitHub Pages
After deployment starts, set:
- Custom domain: www.olamilekanglobalworld.com
- Enable Enforce HTTPS

3. DNS records to add at your domain provider
Use these records:

A records (root domain)
Add 4 A records with these IPs:
- 185.199.108.153
- 185.199.109.153
- 185.199.110.153
- 185.199.111.153

CNAME record
For the subdomain www:
- Name: www
- Type: CNAME
- Value: olalekanb816-cell.github.io

If your provider asks for the root domain:
- use the A records above
- if it asks for www, use the CNAME

4. If your provider supports only one record type
Some providers require:
- An apex/root domain A record set
- And a www CNAME
This is the standard GitHub Pages setup.

5. Important notes
- The repo already contains the correct CNAME file:
  www.olamilekanglobalworld.com
- That file is good and should remain in the root of your repo
- The missing step is enabling Pages and ensuring the DNS points correctly

Example from a provider:
- Record type: A
- Host: @
- Value: 185.199.108.153

Then repeat for the other 3 IPs.

And:
- Record type: CNAME
- Host: www
- Value: olalekanb816-cell.github.io

After DNS propagates, your site should respond at:
- https://www.olamilekanglobalworld.com
- https://olalekanb816-cell.github.io/olamilekanglobalworld/

